    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12-a2">

                <pb facs="0137" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg29"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    390—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Senhor Souza to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of the note which
                    Mr. E. H. Conger, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United
                    States of America, addressed to me on the 7th instant, I have the honor to
                    communicate to him that the Federal Government awaits information from the
                    governors of the States of Bahia and Pernambuco, which it has just sought with
                    urgency, that definite measures may be taken in order that the violations of
                    customs agreement referred to in said note may cease in those States.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. F. Paula
                    Souza.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
